        "path":  "/5379a55",
        "text":  "title: GOT QUESTIONS?",
        "image":  null
    },
    {
        "id":  "77c725d",
        "elType":  "widget",
        "widget":  "text-editor",
        "path":  "/5379a55/9b703bb/07bf7ec",
        "text":  "editor:  Before booking, note where the problem starts, how long it has been happening and whether more than one tap, drain or fixture is affected. These details help H2O Plumbers understand whether it sounds like a leak, blockage, fixture fault or pressure is",
        "image":  null
    },
    {
        "id":  "52b33c5",
        "elType":  "widget",
        "widget":  "text-editor",
        "path":  "/5379a55/9b703bb/f670e8d",
        "text":  "editor:  Leak detection is worth arranging when you notice damp walls, wet cupboards, mould smells, unexplained water use, pressure drops or a meter that moves while taps are closed. Those signs can point to a hidden pipe leak that should be traced before more",
        "image":  null
    },
    {
        "id":  "4b3d608",
        "elType":  "widget",
        "widget":  "text-editor",
        "path":  "/5379a55/9b703bb/7828241",
        "text":  "editor:  A drain that keeps blocking may have grease build-up, root entry, pipe damage, poor fall or a deeper obstruction in the line. Repeated chemical clearing can hide the problem for a short time, but it usually does not deal with the cause.",
        "image":  null
    },
    {
        "id":  "3c037e4",
        "elType":  "widget",
        "widget":  "text-editor",
        "path":  "/5379a55/9b703bb/51dd10c",
        "text":  "editor:  Drain hydro jetting is useful when ordinary drain clearing does not remove the build-up properly. High-pressure water can help clean grease, sludge, debris and some root-related obstruction from the inside of the pipe so flow is restored more thorough",
        "image":  null
    },
    {
        "id":  "8c303b5",
        "elType":  "widget",
        "widget":  "text-editor",
        "path":  "/5379a55/9b703bb/e2d6a31",
        "text":  "editor:  Yes. H2O Plumbers works with residential and commercial clients across the Garden Route, including homes, offices, rental properties, guesthouses and business premises. The team helps with general plumbing, leak detection, blocked drains, core drillin",
        "image":  null
    },
    {
        "id":  "97fa801",
        "elType":  "widget",
        "widget":  "heading",
        "path":  "/adfae7c/48f6af6",
